{
"And the army of Ch'in marched east.": "91736fbd4187",
"At Hsiao there are two ridges. The southern ridge holds the grave of Kao, ruler of Hsia; the northern is where King Wen sheltered from wind and rain.": "1dbc8451efce",
"Besides — march a thousand li, and who will not know of it?": "11fd74269ac5",
"Ch'i-tzu sent word from Cheng to Ch'in: The men of Cheng have put me in charge of the key to their north gate. If you bring an army secretly, the state can be had.": "bac9b694a6b6",
"Chien Shu said: To wear out an army in order to raid a distant place — I have never heard of such a thing.": "d10dfaa4ee3e",
"Chien Shu wept over them, saying: Meng! I see the army go out, but I shall not see it come in.": "584a69eb1694",
"Chien Shu's son was with the army. He wept as he saw him off, saying: The men of Chin will meet the army at Hsiao.": "af2c8b89dbdf",
"Duke Mu consulted Chien Shu about it.": "4f267abad17f",
"The Duke refused him, summoned Meng-ming, Hsi-ch'i and Pai-i, and sent the army out by the east gate.": "289dc1b78590",
"The Duke sent word to him: What do you know? Had you died at the ordinary span, the trees on your grave would be a double handful thick by now.": "970ccea37793",
"The army will be worn out and its strength spent, while the distant ruler will be prepared. Is that not, surely, impossible?": "ac9120cfcb02",
"What the army does, Cheng will certainly know. Toil with nothing to show for it will surely breed mutinous hearts.": "5f004217130b",
"You will die between them. I shall go there to gather your bones.": "ded9abaeefa5"
}
